{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"READ-ONLY DIAGNOSIS from a non-owning session (no claim, no edits, no gates run). Comment only.\n\nQuestion asked: why does scanner-integration actually fail? Answer: there are THREE distinct\nfaults, not two. The third has never been named, and the revert commit's stated diagnosis of it\nis wrong.\n\n== FAULT 1 (already known) — missing script on old-base patchsets ==\ngerrit-verify.yaml resolves the reusable workflow from TRUSTED MAIN but checks out the\nPATCHSET, so `make`/`scripts/` come from the patchset. A patchset whose base predates\n6125c5345f01 has no scripts/install_review_scanners.py.\nMeasured, job 100953010259 (run 33848388672, change 2594/3):\n  python: can't open file '/home/runner/work/rebar/rebar/scripts/install_review_scanners.py':\n  [Errno 2] No such file or directory\nThis explains ONLY the old-base lane.\n\n== FAULT 2 (found, and already fixed on main) — dash has no `pipefail` ==\nMakefile `scanner-integration` opened with `set -euo pipefail`. GNU make runs recipes under\n/bin/sh, which is dash on ubuntu-latest.\nMeasured on MAIN ITSELF, job 100919632441 (workflow_dispatch run 33839813271):\n  review scanner locks: OK\n  /bin/sh: 1: set: Illegal option -o pipefail\n  make: *** [Makefile:475: scanner-integration] Error 2\n  ##[error]Process completed with exit code 2.\nNote `validate-locks` PASSES (\"review scanner locks: OK\"); the failure is the very first line of\nthe make recipe. That is why the job dies in ~30-50s. Also measured on a patchset lane, job\n100941048312. Fixed on main by 6b034b9f8224 (`set -euo pipefail` -> `set -eu`, Makefile:500).\n\n== FAULT 3 (NEW — this is the one nobody had) — dangling RELATIVE semgrep symlink ==\nOnce fault 2 was fixed, the job got further and failed differently. Measured, job 100935522585\n(run 33844923442), against the FIXED Makefile (note \"Makefile:500\", not 475):\n  Successfully installed ... semgrep-1.145.0\n  [notice] To update, run: /home/runner/work/rebar/rebar/.tools/review-scanners/semgrep-venv/bin/python3.12 -m pip install --upgrade pip\n  ERROR: could not execute .tools/review-scanners/bin/semgrep: [Errno 2] No such file or directory: '.tools/review-scanners/bin/semgrep'\n  make: *** [Makefile:500: scanner-integration] Error 2\n\nMechanism, with citations (paths absolute; line numbers as of 6b034b9f8224):\n- /Users/joeoakhart/rebar/Makefile:503 passes a RELATIVE prefix:\n  `--prefix \"$(REVIEW_SCANNER_PREFIX)\"` where REVIEW_SCANNER_PREFIX := .tools/review-scanners\n  (Makefile:52). By contrast /Users/joeoakhart/rebar/scripts/install_review_scanners.py:22\n  DEFAULT_PREFIX is ABSOLUTE (REPO_ROOT-derived).\n- install_scanners (scripts/install_review_scanners.py:342-354):\n    semgrep = _install_semgrep(entry, semgrep_venv or prefix / \"semgrep-venv\")   # line 351\n    semgrep_link = _link_semgrep(semgrep, prefix)                                # line 352\n    _run_version(semgrep_link, entry.semgrep_version)                            # line 354\n  With a relative prefix, `semgrep` is the RELATIVE path\n  `.tools/review-scanners/semgrep-venv/bin/semgrep`.\n- _link_semgrep (scripts/install_review_scanners.py:328-339) does\n  `link.symlink_to(semgrep)` at line 335, where link is\n  `.tools/review-scanners/bin/semgrep`. A relative symlink target is resolved relative to the\n  symlink's OWN DIRECTORY, so the link resolves to\n  `.tools/review-scanners/bin/.tools/review-scanners/semgrep-venv/bin/semgrep` — nonexistent.\n  The symlink is created successfully and DANGLES.\n- _run_version (scripts/install_review_scanners.py:287-297) execs it, catches OSError at 296 and\n  raises `could not execute {binary}: {exc}` — exactly the CI string above.\n- Gitleaks is unaffected because _install_gitleaks uses `shutil.copy2` (a real copy), not a\n  symlink. That is precisely why gitleaks passes and semgrep fails.\n\nReproduced deterministically in a throwaway tmpdir (no repo touched), identical error shape:\n  link target: .t/rs/semgrep-venv/bin/semgrep\n  link exists() -> False\n  could not execute .t/rs/bin/semgrep: [Errno 2] No such file or directory: '.t/rs/bin/semgrep'\n\nIMPORTANT CORRECTION: the revert commit 9c7d78127696 states \"the underlying scanner contract step\n(pytest SCANNER_INTEGRATION_NODES) fails on every change\". That is NOT what the logs show. pytest\nNEVER RAN. Execution died inside the `install` step's own post-install version verification\n(Makefile:503), before the `check` at 504 and before pytest at 506. The scanner contracts are\nuntested, not failing — the distinction matters for the follow-up ticket, because it means we\nstill have zero evidence about whether the nine contracts pass.\n\nThis also explains why nobody caught it locally: `python scripts/install_review_scanners.py\ninstall` with NO --prefix uses the ABSOLUTE DEFAULT_PREFIX and works fine. Only the Makefile path,\nwhich passes a relative prefix, is broken. The bug is latent in every prefix-override call site.\n\n== BRANCH-HEAD `skipped` vs PATCHSET `failure` ==\nNot a clue about conditions/inputs — it is the documented schedule guard.\n/Users/joeoakhart/rebar/.github/workflows/test.yml:77-79:\n    scanner-integration:\n      if: github.event_name != 'schedule'\n      uses: ./.github/workflows/_scanner-integration.yml\nThe branch-head runs being observed are the scheduled main-health runs. Measured: run 33846424069\nhas `event = schedule`, headSha 6b034b9f8224, and reports scanner-integration = skipped —\nalongside `mutation = skipped`, which carries the same guard (test.yml:71-73). The Gerrit lane\n(gerrit-verify.yaml:241-253) has no schedule guard, so it runs and fails. The `skipped` seen in\nthe docs-only Verified route is a THIRD, separate and intentional thing\n(gerrit-verify.yaml:490 asserts scanner-integration.result == 'skipped').\n\n== ON THE TWO ITEMS FLAGGED BY 2595's OWN LLM REVIEW ==\nExamined; both are real defects but NEITHER is this failure.\n- `--install-dir` honoured on install but not check: _selected_prefix\n  (install_review_scanners.py:376-379) IS applied on both paths in main() (:399, :409-410), so\n  the original complaint is stale as written. The live inconsistency is elsewhere:\n  main() line 405 passes `_selected_prefix(args)` to check_scanners, while --check-only at :392\n  also does — consistent. Ruled out as the cause: CI never passes --install-dir.\n- `--semgrep-venv` declared but never read: it IS read, at main():406 -> install_scanners's\n  `semgrep_venv` kwarg (:347, :351). Stale finding. Ruled out: CI never passes it.\n\n== WHAT A CORRECT FIX LOOKS LIKE (not implemented here) ==\nThe minimal, targeted repair is one line in _link_semgrep: make the symlink target absolute.\n    link.symlink_to(semgrep.resolve())      # install_review_scanners.py:335\nBelt-and-braces alternative that fixes the whole class rather than the one site: resolve the\nprefix once at the boundary, e.g. have _selected_prefix (:376) return `.resolve()`, so every\ndownstream path (bin dir, semgrep-venv, gitleaks work dir, the check path) is absolute regardless\nof how the caller spelled --prefix. I'd favour this one; the relative-prefix hazard is latent in\nevery override call site, not just the symlink.\nEither way, add a regression test that invokes the installer with a RELATIVE --prefix from a\ndifferent cwd and asserts the resulting bin/semgrep is executable — that is the exact gap the\nexisting tests miss, since they exercise the absolute DEFAULT_PREFIX.\n\nSeparately, and independent of the symlink: re-landing this lane must not repeat the vacuous\nvote. 6125c5345f01's own Verified run 33831682168 contains 26 jobs and NO scanner-integration\njob, because the Verified lane runs gerrit-verify.yaml from trusted main, which did not yet\ndefine it. Any re-land needs the lane proven green on a real patchset before it becomes required.\n\nAlso still unknown after the fix: whether the nine SCANNER_INTEGRATION_NODES contracts actually\npass. No run has ever reached them. Treat that as open, not as a known failure.\n\nCurrent state at time of writing: main is 9c7d78127696 (\"Revert scanner-integration Verified\ngate\"), which removes the workflow, the script, the locks and the Makefile target, so the\nimmediate freeze is lifted."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1788516005850227001,"uuid":"b6fe83d7-c00c-49bf-87c8-f9ca900942d1"}